      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespacecslt_1acb97e0e477a841d7b9cc6d2982f3e78d" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>size_t</type>
        <definition>size_t cslt::next_pow2</definition>
        <argsstring>(size_t x)</argsstring>
        <name>next_pow2</name>
        <param>
          <type>size_t</type>
          <declname>x</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Round up to next power of 2. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>x</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Value to round up </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Next power of 2 &gt;= x, or 0 if overflow</para>
</simplesect>
Returns the smallest power of 2 that is &gt;= x. Returns 0 if x is too large and would overflow. Returns 1 for x=1, 0 for x=0.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">assert(cslt::next_pow2(15)<sp/>==<sp/>16);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">assert(cslt::next_pow2(16)<sp/>==<sp/>16);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">assert(cslt::next_pow2(17)<sp/>==<sp/>32);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">assert(cslt::next_pow2(1)<sp/>==<sp/>1);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">assert(cslt::next_pow2(0)<sp/>==<sp/>0);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
